      "heading": "How we researched this guide",
      "body": "<p><strong>Everything factual in this guide traces to one of three places: each platform's own published information, the platform's live Trustpilot profile as captured in August 2026, or an authoritative public-health source listed at the end of the page. Where a fact could not be verified, the guide says so rather than estimating.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Prices.</strong> Talkspace's self-pay and psychiatry prices were verified in October 2026 and are quoted exactly. betterhelp's self-pay range and headspace's app prices were not independently verified at the time of writing, so they are described structurally and not quoted.</li>\n<li><strong>Ratings.</strong> Trustpilot scores and review counts are shown as captured from the live profiles - 3.9 across 9,652 reviews for betterhelp, 4.4 across 2,370 for Talkspace, 1.5 across 770 for headspace - including the uncomfortable ones.</li>\n<li><strong>Clinical statements.</strong> Claims about what therapy is and how it works draw on the American Psychological Association and the National Institute of Mental Health, and are kept general; this guide does not quote outcome percentages it cannot source.</li>\n<li><strong>Community feedback.</strong> Where the guide says \"the community feedback we track\", it refers to verified public discussion threads we review and quote on the platform pages, used as a signal of customer experience rather than as clinical evidence.</li>\n<li><strong>Medical review.</strong> Medical and scientific statements across this site are reviewed by a named medical content reviewer under the policy linked above. Prices, rankings and platform selection are editorial and are not part of that review.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This guide is updated when platform prices, insurance coverage or policies change materially. The date at the top of the page is the last substantive update. Found an error? Tell us through the <a href=\"/contact\">contact page</a> with the statement in question, and we will correct it.</p>"
