      "heading": "Quick-start checklist: from today to your first session",
      "body": "<p><strong>If you want to start online therapy this week, this is the whole process in nine steps, in order. Most people can finish the first six in an evening.</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Decide what you need.</strong> A licensed therapist for a clinical concern, a prescriber if medication is plausible, or a daily practice app for stress and sleep. The sections above explain how to tell.</li>\n<li><strong>Ask HR about your EAP.</strong> Free sessions may already be included in your benefits. One email settles it.</li>\n<li><strong>Run the insurance checks.</strong> Talkspace's and betterhelp's eligibility checks take minutes and tell you what you will actually pay. headspace's therapy service has its own coverage check.</li>\n<li><strong>Pick the platform that fits the answer.</strong> Covered platform at copay rates first; otherwise betterhelp for flexible talk therapy, Talkspace for messaging-first or psychiatry, headspace for practice.</li>\n<li><strong>Read the billing and cancellation terms</strong> before entering a card: cycle, pause, cancel, refunds.</li>\n<li><strong>Complete the intake honestly</strong>, including therapist preferences and your exact location.</li>\n<li><strong>Verify the license</strong> on your state board's lookup once you are matched. Two minutes.</li>\n<li><strong>Set up your space and test the technology</strong> the day before: privacy, light, headphones, connection.</li>\n<li><strong>Book sessions two to four in advance</strong>, and save 988 in your phone. Then show up.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Print this list, or screenshot it, and work down it in order. Every step is small and most take minutes; the only genuinely hard one is the first.</p>"
